window.TRIAGE_DATA = {"version": "1.0", "description": "Scale Session triage call script (Mariana-led qualification call before the closer's strategy call with John). Each stage has the verbatim script, a clear goal, green-light criteria the rep must hit before moving on, uncertainty triggers, and the exact pushback script.", "stages": [{"id": "opening", "name": "1. Opening", "tone": "Sit back, relax, speak slowly and calmly.", "goal": "Make sure you know WHY they booked the call. NO PAIN = NO MORE TALKING. Don't move on until you know.", "say": ["Hi [name]. Tell me about your day. (If they're busy: 'Oh [name], is now no longer a good time?')", "Fantastic over here!", "I'm Mariana, I oversee and direct the entire social media and content strategy for Lauren's brand. (For context: I've closed multiple 7 figures in cash for Lauren and I've been with her over the last half decade.)", "I have a note in my calendar that you're interested in generating more revenue from your social media.", "So over the next 10-15 minutes of this call, in an ideal world, what are you most hoping to get out of our conversation together?", "(Let them reply.)", "Ok awesome. From our 7 years in this business, we know that alignment is important to a healthy relationship. So this call may feel pretty basic but that doesn't mean it isn't important because we'll go through a few specifics, to see if we can help. Ok?", "If we can help you, I'll let you know, and we'll arrange a second call to go through things in more detail. And if not, I'll aim to point you in the right direction. Is that ok [name]?", "Ok great. So you know we're all about driving revenue from social media. That's what inspired you to want to speak with us, right?", "(If they don't elaborate on WHY they booked: 'Ok gotcha. So that I can understand your situation, what made you want to decide to book this call with us? What problem are you hoping we can solve?')"], "green_light": ["You know the specific reason they booked the call", "There is a clear pain or goal they want help with"], "pushback_triggers": ["idk", "i don't know", "not sure", "just to learn", "just to see", "just curious", "just exploring", "just to find out", "just wanted to chat", "you reached out", "saw an ad", "lauren reached out", "i was just"], "pushback_script": "IDK what you guys do — How did you end up on this call then? Ok cool no worries then, in an ideal world what would you like to get out of this call?\n\nIf they say 'just to learn more about ___': 'Got it, and I can imagine you're quite busy right?' (PAUSE — let them say yes.) Then half laughing with a smile: 'Yeah. And just so we can see what could best help… Do you go around jumping on calls to learn more all day? Or are you here because you're interested in potentially working with us, if you think it could help?'"}, {"id": "icp", "name": "2. ICP Check", "tone": "Confident — you've already done your homework on their socials.", "goal": "Confirm they're in our ideal client profile. If obviously ICP from their socials (good audience, real business), don't dive deep here.", "say": ["(Check their socials BEFORE the call. If they're obviously ICP, don't dive deep — just say:)", "So first of all, great work building such a big audience. I saw you have [X] followers on [PLATFORM]. Is that where you drive most of your revenue from? Or is there another platform like email or ads where you're bringing in most of your new clients?", "So I did check your [platform] and noticed [problem — e.g. low engagement, big audience but very few comments].", "(And I know you had a brief conversation with Lauren.)", "Is that the main place you're getting your new clients from? Or do you use something else like YouTube, email, ads, LinkedIn?"], "green_light": ["You know which platform drives their revenue", "You've named the specific gap you noticed on their socials"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm not really sure", "i haven't really thought", "i don't really track", "depends", "varies", "a bit of everything", "all over"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept 'a bit of everything' here. Pin it down: 'Got it — but if you had to point to the ONE platform that's bringing in the most revenue right now, which one would it be?' You need a clear answer so the closer knows where they're at."}, {"id": "results", "name": "3. Results & Goal", "tone": "Visionary — paint the picture.", "goal": "Clarity that their goal is a good goal and realistic for us to hit (e.g. add a lot of revenue — more than 10k per month additionally — or get speaking gigs from organic). DO NOT MOVE ON until you are certain they have a goal we can help with.", "say": ["Ok, so let's jump 3 years into the future. Lauren, you and I are at your favourite dinner spot, eating your favourite meal, looking back on the last 3 years celebrating our successful collaboration. What are the top 2 or 3 wins we're celebrating together?", "Love it, that's worth celebrating over. And because we're all about driving revenue with social media, just like a personal trainer would need to know your ideal body shape and fitness goals so we have a target, where exactly would you like to get to revenue wise in 1 year from now, and 3 years from now?", "Cool — that's clear. Thank you. So that I can understand your business better, if that's where you want to be… how far off are you right now from that monthly revenue level?"], "green_light": ["They've named a specific monthly revenue target", "The target is realistic + something we can help with (≥ +10k/mo or speaking gigs from organic)", "You know the gap between current and goal"], "pushback_triggers": ["i don't really know", "haven't thought about it", "not sure what i want", "whatever", "just more", "to be successful", "to grow", "more money", "i'd be happy with anything", "see what happens"], "pushback_script": "This goal isn't clear enough. You can't pass them to the closer with vague goals. Push: 'I hear you — but to make sure we're not wasting your time, I need a specific number. If you could click your fingers and have anything, what's the monthly revenue you'd want to be at in 12 months? Just throw a number at me — there's no wrong answer.' Do not move on until you have a number."}, {"id": "revenue", "name": "4. Current Revenue", "tone": "Curious + non-judgemental.", "goal": "Get clear on their current monthly revenue. Doesn't matter what it is — but important we know so the closer can pitch the right level of support.", "say": ["Ok got it, so your monthly revenue over the last 6 months, what has it been exactly? I ask so that I can see which of our levels of support might make the most sense for you."], "green_light": ["You have a specific monthly revenue figure (or a clear range)"], "pushback_triggers": ["varies", "depends", "it's complicated", "i'd have to check", "i don't track", "ballpark", "give or take", "around"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept vague here. The closer needs a real number. Push gently: 'Totally get it varies — but over the last 6 months on average, what would you say it's been per month? Doesn't have to be exact, just a real ballpark so I can match you to the right level of support.' Hold for the answer."}, {"id": "past-attempts", "name": "5. Past Attempts", "tone": "Curious — chase what they liked/disliked.", "goal": "List down how they want to get support and pass it to the closer. Doesn't matter what they say but it's important we know.", "say": ["Have you worked with anyone else or any other companies to help with this before?", "(Let them reply.)", "What did you like or dislike about it?", "Thank you for sharing. What attracted you to the Scale Systems way of doing things? What did you like about our method specifically?", "(IF they say they have a coach OR are working with someone else now:)", "Got you, seeing as you're already working with someone else — what's not working as well as it should be that means you're interested in working with us?"], "green_light": ["You know if they've worked with similar companies before", "You know what attracted them to Scale Systems specifically", "If they have a current coach: you know what's not working"], "pushback_triggers": ["no idea", "not sure why", "just thought i'd see", "we just heard", "lauren's posts"], "pushback_script": "If they can't articulate what attracted them to us, that's a soft answer. Push: 'Got it — but specifically, was it the AI content angle, the revenue focus, something Lauren said? Just so I know what most resonated with you.' This helps the closer hit the right angle."}, {"id": "time", "name": "6. Time & Urgency", "tone": "Direct — you're qualifying their commitment.", "goal": "Get clear they have ~1 hour per day and they want help NOW. If they don't, note it for the closer but pass them through anyway — the closer can overcome it.", "say": ["Got it. So how much time do you have to focus on driving revenue into your business per day?", "Right and how soon are you looking to get help with this?", "The reason I ask is that we have a couple of specific offers on right now, so I just want to ensure the timing is good for you to get support from us if we can help. Would there be any obstacles that would prevent you from moving forwards if we felt like it was a fit?"], "green_light": ["You know they have at least 1 hour per day", "They've said they want help now (not 'someday')", "You know any obstacles upfront"], "pushback_triggers": ["no rush", "no hurry", "whenever", "sometime", "we'll see", "depends", "maybe in a few months", "later in the year", "next year", "not in a rush", "no specific timeline", "when's good for you"], "pushback_script": "Stalling on urgency. Push with the qualifier: 'Got it, and if you were certain this would add decent revenue to your business on a monthly basis, would that change things?' (ONLY use this if they aren't financially qualified or are giving a BS answer.) Even if they're still stalling, pass them through to the closer — closer can overcome this. But make sure the closer knows they aren't rushing to move forward now, so the closer can prepare."}, {"id": "budget", "name": "7. Budget", "tone": "Anchored + confident. You're not negotiating — you're stating the range.", "goal": "Get a real number from them OR confirm the 2k-6k/month range works. If they give a low number you think they could stretch, run the stretch question.", "say": ["Got it. So your goal of [X] is clear, and I understand you're interested in working with us because of [pain].", "So how much have you set aside to invest in getting this working.", "Most people in your position typically invest between **2k to 6k a month** to see results like you're looking for. Does that align with what you're prepared for?", "STRETCH (if they give a low number but you feel they could do more): 'And if you knew that this would allow you to [insert problems they have], would you be able to stretch that?'", "IF THEY SAY 'I could do that on a payment plan': Get the exact amount they could do. 'Cool, so 1-6k per month wouldn't be an issue for you if you were sure it'd work?'"], "green_light": ["They've confirmed 2k-6k/month aligns OR", "They've given a specific real number you can pass to the closer"], "pushback_triggers": ["i don't really have a budget", "depends what it is", "we'd need to figure", "it depends", "how much is it", "i need to know more", "i can't say", "i don't know", "varies", "what would you suggest", "tell me the price", "i don't have a number", "hard to say"], "pushback_script": "Hhhhmmm okay OR Got it — and so we can see which of our options could be feasible, on a monthly basis, what are you willing to invest to be sure you'd get this working?\n\nIf they STILL won't give a number — push once more: 'Just throw out a real number, even if it's a rough one. There's no wrong answer — it just helps me match you to the right tier.' Don't move on without a number you can pass to the closer."}, {"id": "authority", "name": "8. Authority", "tone": "Half laughing on the close — light but pinning it down.", "goal": "Surface every decision-maker now so the closer doesn't get blindsided by a spouse / accountant / business partner objection.", "say": ["Ok thank you. So for your social media, do you have someone on your team who helps with any of this? Like a VA or an appointment setter or something?", "And is there anyone else involved in making decisions when it comes to your business or is that something you have full autonomy over?", "(If they say 'just me' — say this half laughing:)", "Ok got it, so you're not going to hit us with an objection like 'I need to speak to my partner?' or 'I have to run this by my accountant?' right?"], "green_light": ["You know who else is in the decision (spouse, partner, accountant, team)", "OR you've pinned down it's just them and they've confirmed no surprise stakeholders"], "pushback_triggers": ["well, i do need to", "i'd probably want to", "i might need to check", "let me think about that", "i'd run it by", "i'd want to talk to", "we make decisions together", "i'd want to consult", "i'd discuss"], "pushback_script": "They just surfaced a hidden decision-maker. Pin it down NOW so the closer isn't ambushed: 'Got it — who specifically, and what would they need to be comfortable with for this to be a yes?' Note it for the closer. A hidden stakeholder kills the close."}, {"id": "fit-qualified", "name": "9a. Fit — Pass to Closer", "tone": "[SLOW + CONFIDENT TONALITY]", "goal": "Book the strategy call with John (closer) and hold them accountable to watching the pre-call doc.", "say": ["Cool. So with what you're looking to do, it's a pretty straightforward problem for us to solve.", "Now I am going to get you to have a 1:1 interview with Lauren's business partner directly, John, to go through the details and specifics on how it'll work for you, to ensure you [overcome the problem they have].", "(*Act like you are looking at a jam-packed calendar with 0 availability*)", "So I'm just looking at John's calendar here… Okk… hmm.. So John's calendar is really full…", "Now, what I can do, because you're looking to work with us… is I can move a few things around for you… Would [X] or [Y] time work best for you? Then I'll be able to get you in directly with Lauren's business partner.", "▸ BOOK THE TIME HERE WITH CLOSER.", "Great — you mentioned earlier that you run decisions by [x], so what's their email address so I can invite them to the next call?", "(Let them reply.)", "Ok great. I am booking that now for you…. [3 seconds]", "You should have received a confirmation email by now, did you get that? (Make sure they check.)", "Ok great so now I'm sending you a document which breaks down our offer and how it works. It's really important you watch that, because when you speak with John he'll be able to break down, for YOU, how this system will work when applied specifically to your business.", "John is really busy — so if you can't go through that before your call with him, can you let me know now? (Get confirmation they can watch it before.)", "Ok great — when are you planning to watch it, so I can check in with you to make sure you've been able to go through it in full, and confirm your call with John?", "Ok cool — I will hold you accountable to that. So expect a call or text from me right around then!", "Just a note, your strategy session will take place on a google meet link, not a phone call. So please make sure you are somewhere quiet, where you can focus. Sounds ok?", "It's been great chatting today — I'll be waiting for your reply to that email confirming you've been through the doc."], "green_light": ["Strategy call booked + on the calendar", "Confirmation email received + they checked", "They committed to a specific time they'll watch the doc", "They confirmed they can be on a google meet (not phone)"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'll try", "if i have time", "i'll see", "maybe", "i'll do my best", "we'll see how it goes", "i'll get to it", "no promises"], "pushback_script": "They just gave you a soft commitment on watching the doc. Don't accept it. Push: 'John is really busy — so if you can't go through that before your call with him, can you let me know now?' Get a hard yes or move the call. A soft yes here = a no-show or unprepared prospect, which wastes John's time and burns the opportunity."}, {"id": "fit-disqualified", "name": "9b. Fit — Lauren Follow-up (not qualified)", "tone": "Warm — they're not going to John, but Lauren will reach out personally.", "goal": "Pass them to Lauren via DM follow-up. Confirm they're following her on the right platform and they'll be on phone to receive her message.", "say": ["Cool. So with what you're looking to do, it's a pretty straightforward problem for us to solve.", "Now, what I'm going to do for you is, I'll have a conversation with Lauren later today about everything we discussed here, and she'll personally reach out to you to send you the solution that's more aligned with what you're looking to do, which is [X, Y, Z].", "I understand you are more active on [SOCIAL MEDIA PLATFORM], so she'll be reaching out there, just to confirm and make sure you'll get her message — you know that sometimes it can land in the request folder, are you following her there?", "(Let them reply — and make sure you check on your end in case they're lying about it.)", "Okay perfect, could you send her a message now for me? I have a meeting with her right after this call so that way she can check your full profile and reach out to you in a few minutes, to make sure to cover all of your questions before getting you started.", "Lauren checks her DMs a couple of times per day. What times later today could you be on your phone to have a chat with her?"], "green_light": ["Confirmed they follow Lauren on the right platform (you verified)", "They sent Lauren a DM during the call", "They named a time later today they'll be on their phone"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'll follow her later", "i'll find her", "i'll search", "yeah i think so", "probably", "maybe", "i should be"], "pushback_script": "Make them do it NOW — don't let 'I'll do it later' slide. 'Cool — can you follow her right now while we're on, just so I know it's done?' Then verify on your end. People who say they'll do it later don't."}], "uncertainty_globals": {"version": "1.0", "description": "Global uncertainty signals that always fire as a generic PUSH BACK alert, on top of stage-specific triggers.", "signals": ["let me think about it", "i'll get back to you", "let me sleep on it", "i need to think", "give me some time", "circle back", "send me the info", "send me a proposal", "send me a brochure", "send me everything", "i'll let you know", "we'll see", "tbd", "to be determined"], "alert": "Generic stall language. Don't move on. Push for specifics: 'Got it — but to be fair to your time, can you give me a clearer answer now so I can either get you to the right next step or save us both the time?' Then re-ask the question of the current section."}, "dm_workflow": {"goal": "Book 3 QUALIFIED sales calls per day, of which 2/week become Accelerator members and 50% of the rest become Skool paying clients.", "stages": [{"id": "dm-opener", "name": "1. Opener", "tone": "Light, fast, casual.", "goal": "Hook them with a low-friction email ask + position you have multiple versions based on stage. Goal is to get their email + their stage in 2 messages.", "say": ["MESSAGE 1: lemme get that to you. what is your best email address?", "MESSAGE 2: and I have a few versions so can you tell me what stage of business you're at? 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out — then I can send over the relevant one.", "ADAPT — drop a quick personal line first based on their bio / what they commented. e.g. 'HipHopTV's vision is cool. Media companies are the way forward. Smart move…' then go into Message 2.", "If you also connected on LinkedIn, slip in: 'Just accepted your connection request also :)'"], "green_light": ["You got their email", "You got their stage of business", "Logged in the CRM for follow-up (in case they ghost)"], "pushback_triggers": ["what document", "what is it", "what's the doc", "what link", "what video", "what do you do", "what do you guys do", "tell me more"], "pushback_script": "Don't get pulled into explaining — keep them on the hook. Just say: 'It's a doc that breaks down exactly what we do based on your stage of business. So can you tell me — 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out? Then I'll send you the one that fits.' Bring them back to the email + stage ask."}, {"id": "dm-get-stage", "name": "2. Get Stage (if email-only)", "tone": "Friendly nudge.", "goal": "If they only sent their email and didn't say their stage, loop back with one short line.", "say": ["cool, and what is your stage? 😊", "cool and what is your stage?", "and I have a few versions so can you tell me what stage of business you're at? 6 figures, 7+ figures, or just starting out — then I can send over the relevant one."], "green_light": ["You got their stage (just starting / pre-6 figs / 6 figs / mid 6 figs / 7+ figs)", "Logged in CRM (Message 2 sent)"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm not sure what stage", "depends what you mean", "ish", "kind of in between", "we just started", "varies"], "pushback_script": "Push gently: 'No worries — just throw out a rough monthly revenue or annual range, even if it's not exact. That way I can match you to the right version.' Get a number, not a vibe."}, {"id": "dm-starting-out", "name": "3a. Response — Starting out / 5 figs", "tone": "Encouraging but direct.", "goal": "Pivot from stage → their stuck point. Give them a list of options to anchor the reply.", "say": ["ok cool, in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others start out successfully. what part of it are you the most stuck on? getting leads, getting yourself out there, sales, automations, or something else?"], "green_light": ["You know which part of their business they're stuck on"], "pushback_triggers": ["everything", "all of it", "i don't know where to start", "no idea", "honestly i'm lost"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept 'everything'. Pin one: 'I hear you — but if you HAD to pick the one that hurts the most right now, which would it be? Leads, sales, getting yourself out there, or automations?' One stuck point is enough to book."}, {"id": "dm-pre-6", "name": "3b. Response — not yet at 6 figs", "tone": "Validate the gap between good + traction.", "goal": "Anchor the goood-but-no-traction angle, then ask about their stuck point.", "say": ["ok cool, in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others get over that hurdle of being GOOOD at what you do, but lacking the traction to hit 6 figs. what part of it are you the most stuck on? getting leads, getting yourself out there, sales, automations, or something else?"], "green_light": ["You know their specific traction gap (leads / visibility / sales / automations / other)"], "pushback_triggers": ["everything", "all of it", "i don't know", "lots of things"], "pushback_script": "Pin one: 'If you HAD to pick the single biggest thing keeping you from 6 figs, what would it be?' Then go from there."}, {"id": "dm-6-figs", "name": "3c. Response — 6 figs", "tone": "Peer-to-peer, scale conversation.", "goal": "Position the 6→7 figs angle, ask about their specific scale lever.", "say": ["in that case I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you seeing as we've helped 100s and 100s of others start out successfully and scale from 6 to 7 figs. which part do you think you need support on to get from 6 to 7 figs so I can see what we got? client acquisition, automating more, or hiring?", "MID 6 FIGS ADAPT: 'Given your business stage, plus the calibre of clientele you're working with, I probably have a bunch of other stuff that could help you. What are you currently looking to use LinkedIn for? Getting leads, sales, client retention, finding partners or something else? Then I can see what I may have which might serve you best.'", "HITLIST RULE: any 6 figs+ prospect goes onto the 6-Figures+ Hitlist immediately, regardless of whether they reply. Goal = book a call. Cadence is in the Follow Up stage."], "green_light": ["You know their 6→7 figs lever (acquisition / automation / hiring / other)", "Added to the 6-Figures+ Hitlist"], "pushback_triggers": ["we're doing fine", "not really stuck", "everything's good", "no specific issue"], "pushback_script": "If they're 6 figs and 'doing fine', flip it: 'Got it — so if you could magically fix ONE thing that would make scaling to 7 figs easier, what would it be?' Find the lever even if they downplay."}, {"id": "dm-get-problem", "name": "4. Get Problem → Book Call", "tone": "Move quickly. Goal is the call.", "goal": "Once they name their problem, book the call right away. If they ghost, send a voice memo.", "say": ["oh, well we should find a time to chat for 5 or 10 mins this week. Which day would work?", "we can see how we can help with that in a way that is a no brainer for you"], "green_light": ["Call time confirmed and on the calendar", "OR if they ghosted: voice memo sent"], "pushback_triggers": ["i'm busy", "no time this week", "let me check", "i'll get back", "send me more info first", "what would it cost", "how much", "send me the link"], "pushback_script": "Don't let them push you into more info-dumping. Soft re-anchor: 'totally get it — 5 or 10 mins, just to see if we can help in a way that's a no-brainer for you. would [day] or [day] this week work?' Two specific options force a yes/no. If still ghosting → voice memo."}, {"id": "dm-send-training", "name": "5. Send AI Training (casual)", "tone": "Casual drop, no pitch.", "goal": "Alternative track — drop the AI training link if the call isn't happening yet. Soft soft.", "say": ["Lauren UTM: here's the link for the AI training: https://scalesystems.io/you-ai-start-org?utm_source=Facebook&utm_medium=DMs&utm_campaign=lauren", "Mariana UTM: here's the link for the AI training: https://scalesystems.io/you-ai-start-org?utm_source=Facebook&utm_medium=DMs&utm_campaign=Mariana"], "green_light": ["Link sent with the right UTM (lauren / Mariana)"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback here — casual drop, no commentary."}, {"id": "dm-no-reply", "name": "6. No-Reply Recovery", "tone": "Light, no pressure.", "goal": "Soft re-engage if they've gone silent. One short line.", "say": ["If it's easier you can find a time here: [LINK]"], "green_light": ["Re-engagement message sent"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "If they reply with stall language to this, jump into Follow-Up cadence."}, {"id": "dm-follow-up", "name": "7. Follow Up + Hitlist", "tone": "Personal + genuine. No sales-y.", "goal": "Two parallel cadences. NORMAL list: run the 3-touch weekly hitlist (voice memo -> value-add -> personal feedback). 6-FIGURES+ HITLIST: every 3rd day for 2 weeks with 1:1 value-add follow-up, then once per month indefinitely, PLUS a weekly broadcast email to the separate Hitlist email list. Goal of the hitlist = book a call.", "say": ["NORMAL list — 3-touch weekly hitlist for prospects who DM'd but didn't convert:", "  Touch 1 — Voice memo: personal + casual, reference what they said before. Under 30 seconds.", "  Touch 2 — Value-add: a video that helps with their specific problem. No ask attached.", "  Touch 3 — Personal feedback: one piece of feedback specifically for them (like Lauren did with Pierre). Genuinely useful, not pitchy.", "6-FIGURES+ HITLIST — separate, prioritised list. Goal = book a call.", "  1:1 cadence: send a value-add follow-up every 3rd day for the first 2 weeks, then once per month indefinitely until they book or ask to be removed.", "  Broadcast cadence: they also go on a SEPARATE weekly email list — one tailored email per week, specific to the hitlist (not the main newsletter).", "  Log every touch in the CRM. If they reply with a problem, book the call right away (jump to Get Problem -> Book Call)."], "green_light": ["NORMAL: Touch 1 (voice memo) sent", "NORMAL: Touch 2 (value video) sent", "NORMAL: Touch 3 (personal feedback) sent", "6 FIGS+: scheduled into 1:1 every-3rd-day cadence (2 weeks)", "6 FIGS+: added to weekly hitlist broadcast email list", "All touches logged in CRM"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback — these touches are value-only. If after all 3 they still don't engage, they go cold for now."}], "style_rule": "MIRROR THEIR STYLE every time. If they use capitalisation and proper grammar, you do too. If they use emojis, you do too. If they write lowercase + casual, match that. Match their energy, register, and length. Every DM is personalised to the prospect — the templates are a starting point, not a copy-paste.", "crm_rule": "EVERY prospect you message gets logged in the CRM after Message 1 (so you remember to follow up if they ghost), and again after Message 2. If they're 6 figures or above, ALSO add them to the 6-Figures+ Hitlist (see Follow Up stage for the cadence)."}, "outbound_workflow": {"goal": "Dial leads who opted into our freebies (YOU-AI training, etc.) within 24 hours of opt-in. Pattern-interrupt opener, get a real problem in 60 seconds, book the call or send the AI training and follow up. Verbatim-style is Matt Ryder — flag any line below for refinement once we mine his outbound-specific videos.", "style_rule": "Tonality is EVERYTHING on outbound. Low-energy, conversational, almost friendly. Don't sound like a salesperson. Short sharp questions ('what do you mean?' / 'how long?' / 'why's that?') — never the long 'so what I'm hearing you say is…' robot phrasing. If you sound surprised to be on the phone with them, they'll mirror it and stay on. Smile while you dial — they hear it.", "stages": [{"id": "ob-opener", "name": "1. Pattern Interrupt", "tone": "Low-energy, slightly informal — like you bumped into them at a coffee shop.", "goal": "Disarm them in the first 5 seconds so they don't hang up. The 'weird' intro is the move — it breaks their 'this is a sales call' pattern.", "say": ["Hey [name], it's [you] from Lauren Tickner's team — got a really quick odd question for you, you got 20 seconds?", "(Alt:) Hey [name], it's [you] — this is going to sound a bit random, but you got 30 seconds?", "(If they push back 'what's this about?'): Totally fair — I'll be super quick. You grabbed our [freebie] the other day, just wanted to ask you one thing about that. 20 seconds tops?"], "green_light": ["They said yes / kept the line open", "You haven't been hung up on"], "pushback_triggers": ["what's this about", "who is this", "is this a sales call", "i'm busy", "i'm not interested", "take me off", "not a good time"], "pushback_script": "Stay calm, stay low energy. Don't get defensive. Just say: 'Totally fair — and I get the call out of nowhere is weird. You grabbed our [freebie] the other day, that's why I'm reaching out. I'll be 20 seconds tops — can I ask you one thing about it?' If they still say no: 'No worries — would it be easier if I sent you a quick text instead?' Then send a soft follow-up DM/text."}, {"id": "ob-hook", "name": "2. Hook to the Opt-in", "tone": "Curious — you genuinely want to know.", "goal": "Anchor the call to the specific freebie they grabbed, then surface what made them grab it.", "say": ["Just saw you grabbed our [YOU-AI training / AI freebie / whichever], a few days ago. Out of curiosity — what made you grab that one specifically? Is there something specific you're trying to figure out right now?", "(Soft follow-on if they downplay): Got it — and have you actually had a chance to go through it yet, or is it still in the queue?"], "green_light": ["They named what made them grab the freebie", "You know if they've consumed it or not"], "pushback_triggers": ["just curious", "just wanted to see", "no specific reason", "i grab everything", "lauren's stuff is good", "just for fun"], "pushback_script": "Don't accept 'just curious'. Push softly with curiosity: 'Got it — but if you had to point to one thing, what specifically caught your eye? Was it the AI angle, the revenue thing, something Lauren said? Just wondering.' There's always a reason — find it."}, {"id": "ob-problem", "name": "3. Surface the Problem", "tone": "Curious, no pressure — short sharp questions only.", "goal": "Get one specific problem in their own words. NOT a sales pitch — just a real problem you can hook the call to.", "say": ["Cool. So when you say [X] — what do you mean by that?", "How long has that been the case?", "Has that put you in a tough position? In what way?", "(If they go vague:) Tell me more.", "(If they say 'I'm not sure'): What's the bit that's most frustrating right now?"], "green_light": ["You have one specific, named problem in their words", "You know roughly how long it's been a problem", "You have a sense of the cost (time / money / energy)"], "pushback_triggers": ["i don't know", "everything", "all of it", "no real issue", "it's not that bad", "fine i guess", "depends"], "pushback_script": "Stay short and curious — DO NOT switch into pitch mode. Just one more probe: 'Got it — and if you HAD to pick the single biggest thing you'd want fixed, what would it be?' If they still won't name it, they're either not ready or you have to come back later. Don't force it — book a future check-in instead."}, {"id": "ob-stage", "name": "4. Stage Qualifier", "tone": "Light, matter-of-fact.", "goal": "Get their stage of business so you know which offer to set up. Same buckets as DMs.", "say": ["Just so I can point you in the right direction — what stage of business are you at right now? Just starting out, 6 figs, 7+ figs?"], "green_light": ["Stage confirmed (starting / pre-6 / 6 figs / mid-6 / 7+)"], "pushback_triggers": ["depends", "kind of in between", "ish", "we just started", "varies"], "pushback_script": "Pin a number: 'Cool — what's your rough monthly revenue right now? Doesn't have to be exact, just a ballpark.' Get a number, not a vibe."}, {"id": "ob-book", "name": "5. Book the Call", "tone": "Confident — you're offering them something, not asking permission.", "goal": "Book a 15-min call with the triage rep (Mariana) or the closer (John) this week. Two options force a decision.", "say": ["Cool — based on what you told me, this is actually exactly the kind of thing we help [stage] businesses with. We should jump on a quick 15-min call this week with [Mariana / one of the team] to walk you through what's working for people in your spot and see if it'd fit you. What's better — Tuesday or Thursday?", "(If they say yes to a day:) Cool, [morning or afternoon]? ... Alright, [time] it is. What's the best email so I can fire over the invite right now while we're on?", "Just so you're set up: it's a Google Meet (not a phone call). Make sure you can be somewhere quiet with no distractions. Sound good?", "Last thing — I'll send you a quick doc to watch before the call. It'll mean way more once we're on. Cool to give that 10 mins before we meet?"], "green_light": ["Call booked + on the calendar (you SAW it land in the calendar)", "They confirmed the email + got the invite", "They committed to watching the doc before", "They confirmed they can be on Google Meet (not phone)"], "pushback_triggers": ["let me check my calendar", "i'll get back to you", "i'm not sure i can", "what's the cost", "how much is it", "what's it going to cost", "send me more info", "send me a link", "maybe next week", "i need to think"], "pushback_script": "DO NOT let them push you into more info. The call IS the info. Just say: 'Totally get it — and to be straight, the call is just 15 mins, no pitch. We literally just walk through your situation and see if it makes sense to keep talking. So — Tuesday or Thursday this week? Even a tentative slot is fine, you can always move it.' Two specific options force a yes/no. If still stalling: 'Cool, can I send you the AI training in the meantime and circle back in a couple of days?' Then put them on the hitlist (if 6 figs+) or the normal follow-up list."}, {"id": "ob-voicemail", "name": "6. Voicemail / No Answer", "tone": "Quick + casual, like leaving a voice note to a friend.", "goal": "Drop a short voicemail that gets a callback — under 20 seconds.", "say": ["Hey [name], it's [you] from Lauren Tickner's team — just saw you grabbed our [freebie], wanted to ask you a quick question about what brought you there. Give me a quick text or call back at [number] when you've got 20 seconds. Cool, talk soon.", "(Immediately after the voicemail — send a follow-up DM/text on the same channel they opted in on):", "Hey [name] — just left you a quick voicemail re: the [freebie] you grabbed. Couple of seconds when you've got a sec? — [you]"], "green_light": ["Voicemail left (short — under 20 sec)", "Follow-up text/DM sent on the channel they opted in on", "Lead logged in CRM for retry"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback for voicemails — just leave a short one and move to follow-up."}, {"id": "ob-followup", "name": "7. Outbound Follow-Up", "tone": "Genuine, low pressure, value-led.", "goal": "Standard outbound follow-up cadence for opt-in dialers who didn't pick up or book. If they're 6 figs+ they go on the 6-Figures+ Hitlist (same as DMs).", "say": ["Day 0 — Dial + voicemail + text (above).", "Day 2 — Re-dial at a different time. If no answer: short text 'still keen to chat about [the thing they downloaded]? happy to send you a quick doc instead.'", "Day 4 — Send the AI training link casually via text/DM (no ask, just value).", "Day 7 — Final dial + voice memo: 'Hey [name] — couple of attempts to catch you, no pressure. If now's not the right time totally fine, just let me know if you'd rather we circle back in a few weeks.'", "IF 6 FIGURES+ → move them onto the 6-Figures+ Hitlist after Day 7 (every 3rd day value-add for 2 weeks, then once per month indefinitely + weekly hitlist email). Goal = book the call.", "ALL touches logged in CRM."], "green_light": ["Day 0 / 2 / 4 / 7 touches completed in order", "All logged in CRM", "If 6 figs+: moved onto Hitlist after Day 7"], "pushback_triggers": [], "pushback_script": "No pushback — cadence runs regardless of replies. If they reply with a problem, jump to Surface Problem -> Book Call."}]}};
